{"cases":[{"attack":true,"case":"The claim asserts separation is 'strictly necessary' for independent verification, but its own countercondition admits execution-based verification (where ground truth is external) makes the engine's bias irrelevant. The problem asks what distinguishes genuine independent verification from restatement; an execution-based check (e.g., running code) would be independent verification despite same-engine authoring, refuting strict necessity. Count: run the authored code; if it passes, independent verification occurred without separation.","counterexample":["Run the authoring engine's code to verify the claim; the environment's ground truth provides independent verification despite shared weights."],"target":"0dcfd009d4ed7222b76db11b5bc043c4f62f10d48c3beb14df5d21d7d57e9600"},{"attack":true,"case":"The claim asserts strict necessity, but its countercondition admits a formal mathematical proof verified by a deterministic mechanical check (e.g., Lean kernel) constitutes verification where the probabilistic semantic check is bypassed. The problem explicitly asks for what to count or execute; executing the Lean kernel verifies the proof independently despite same-engine authoring, refuting strict necessity. Execute: run the Lean kernel on the proof.","counterexample":["Execute a Lean kernel on the authoring engine's formal proof; the deterministic check provides independent verification without engine separation."],"target":"182fb4ce1edae04155d5fa4600733ba474cc22fd08fd0493a1d9dbfc55aa29c4"},{"attack":true,"case":"The target's overturn conditions require proof that shared weights create an inescapable 'semantic blind spot' regardless of context. The problem asks to identify what evidence distinguishes genuine independent verification from restatement and to specify what to count or execute. An execution-based verification (e.g., running code or counting results) within the same run would provide independent verification even with shared weights, because the environment—not the engine—acts as checker. Execute: run the authored code and count passing/failing assertions; a pass is independent verification without separation, overturning the inescapability claim.","counterexample":["Execute the authored code within the same run and count passing assertions; the environment provides independent verification despite shared weights."],"target":"6aa546f067bbd278752df29bebc2c4f42e2b544a89d0d48e3980df5d8e840c33"}]}